      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/31/5296",
      "text": [
        ": سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ اَلسِّنِّ وَ اَلذِّرَاعِ يُكْسَرَانِ عَمْداً أَ لَهُمَا أَرْشٌ أَوْ قَوَدٌ فَقَالَ \"قَوَدٌ\"\nقَالَ قُلْتُ فَإِنْ أَضْعَفُوا لَهُ اَلدِّيَةَ فَقَالَ \"إِنْ أَرْضَوْهُ بِمَا شَاءَ فَهُوَ لَهُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5296 - It is narrated by Asim ibn Humaid from Abu Basir from Abu Abdullah (as) who said: I asked Imam (as) about a tooth or an arm that is intentionally broken - does it require compensation (financial payment) or is there retaliation (qisas)?\nImam (as) replied: \"Retaliation (qisas).\"\nI asked: \"What if they offer him blood money instead?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"If he is satisfied with whatever they offer, then it is permissible for him.\""
        ]
      }
